weewx-sds011
Copyright 2021- sbsRouteur
Copyright 2019 Matthew Wall
Distributed under the terms of GPLv3; see license.

Read PM2.5 and PM10 mass concentrations from a Nova SDS011 particulate sensor
over a serial connection. The module offers a WeeWX station driver and a
service that adds pm2_5 and pm10_0 to an existing driver's LOOP packets.

This repository mirrors [sbsrouteur/weewx-sds011](https://github.com/sbsrouteur/weewx-sds011).
Use the separately repaired catalog archive `0.2.post20261022` below.
A source-branch ZIP does not include those packaging repairs. The catalog repair preserves serial protocol octets on Python 3.

Installation

For a pip installation, activate the existing virtual environment that runs
your WeeWX service before running these commands. Both `python` and `weectl`
must come from that environment. For a distribution package installation, use
its `weectl`, with `sudo` if required. Add `--config /path/to/weewx.conf` to the
extension command when your station configuration is not found automatically.

For Debian or Raspberry Pi OS package installations, use
`sudo apt install python3-serial` instead of pip. The pip command below is for
WeeWX running in its existing virtual environment.

Use WeeWX 5.5–5.x, Python 3.10–3.14 and pyserial in the WeeWX environment:

python -m pip install 'pyserial'

Install the published archive with WeeWX 5's extension installer:

```sh
weectl extension install https://github.com/weewx-packages/catalog/releases/download/sds011/v0.2.post20261022/sds011-0.2.post20261022.tar.gz
```

Restart your WeeWX service after configuration, for example
`sudo systemctl restart weewx` on systemd. The installer does not restart it
for you.

The installer copies bin/user/sds011.py and adds pm_binding with a pm.sdb
configuration. It does not register a service or select the station driver.
The binding alone does not collect or save readings to a separate PM database.
Choose one of the following modes.

Use alongside an existing weather station

Keep your current Station section. Append user.sds011.SDS011Extension to the
existing data_services list in [Engine][[Services]]. Preserve all existing
services. This service reads its options at the TOP LEVEL of weewx.conf:

port = /dev/ttyUSB0
timeout = 3
poll_interval = 30
max_tries = 3
retry_wait = 5

[Engine]
    [[Services]]
        # Append user.sds011.SDS011Extension to the existing data_services value.

Place those scalar options before the first section. A [SDS011] section does
not configure this service. Use a port accessible to the WeeWX account.
The sensor uses 9600 baud. pm2_5 and pm10_0 need matching columns in the main
archive if you want them stored. Restart WeeWX after editing configuration.

Use as the station driver

For a station dedicated to the SDS011, select:

[Station]
    station_type = SDS011
[SDS011]
    driver = user.sds011
    port = /dev/ttyUSB0
    poll_interval = 30

Do not also enable SDS011Extension for the same device. The driver configuration
editor is available through weectl station reconfigure --driver user.sds011.

Operation and limits

Check the WeeWX log for serial access and readings. Poll no faster than once
per 10 seconds. The service performs synchronous serial reads/retries in its
LOOP callback, enables WeeWX debugging and prints timing information.
Its exhausted-retry path still references an undefined method variable;
serial failures can therefore raise NameError. The catalog serial-byte repair
does not change those service behaviours. No physical sensor was used for the
documentation checks.

For available diagnostic options, run this without opening the device:

PYTHONPATH=/path/to/station/bin python -m user.sds011 --help

Upgrade or remove

Back up configuration and databases before installing a newer fixed archive.
Remove manually added service/driver configuration when uninstalling with
weectl extension uninstall sds011, then restart WeeWX. Keep a working station
driver configured.
